# ECC Optimizations (GoalChain)

Maintain maximum execution speed and token efficiency across all agent sessions.

## 1. Token Optimization & Context Control

- **Slim Contexts:** Keep file reads targeted. Avoid reading entire files unless absolutely necessary.
- **Hook Profile:** Set `ECC_HOOK_PROFILE=minimal` to prevent heavy pre/post hooks from bloating your session context.
- **Limit Start Context:** Use `ECC_SESSION_START_CONTEXT=off` to avoid dumping large history files on startup.
- **Disable Heavy MCPs:** Ensure heavy unused MCP servers (`canva`, `github`, `filesystem`) are disabled to avoid background CPU/Memory drag.

## 2. Memory Persistence & Pruning

- **Pruning:** Maintain SQLite databases and old session logs by settting `ECC_SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS=7`.
- **Memory Trimming:** Regularly run `ops/hermes/trim-hermes-memory.sh` to keep `MEMORY.md` under limits.
- **Agent Data Boundary:** Keep Cursor and Claude Code session data isolated by setting `ECC_AGENT_DATA_HOME="$HOME/.cursor/ecc"`.

## 3. High-Throughput Verification Loops

- **Local Compilation:** Always rebuild SDK (`cd goalchain-sdk && npm run build`) before compiling dependent packages.
- **Targeted Testing:** Run localized tests (`npm test` in the touched package directory) instead of full monorepo runs.
- **Grader Checks:** Review changes for lint warnings and type safety before submitting.
